WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.562 --> 00:00:04.646
[Bear] And, oh, oh, here he is.

00:00:06.732 --> 00:00:08.734
[Gordon Ramsay] That's a
massive barracuda.

00:00:08.817 --> 00:00:10.569
[Bear] Come on.

00:00:14.698 --> 00:00:17.034
[Gordon Ramsay] Come on.
Come on, baby.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:17.909
[Bear] Drop it, drop it,
drop it, drop it,

00:00:18.076 --> 00:00:19.745
drop it, drop it, drop it.
Let him eat it.

00:00:19.911 --> 00:00:21.830
[Gordon Ramsay] Take it.

00:00:22.247 --> 00:00:23.415
Now he's on. He's got it.

00:00:23.498 --> 00:00:24.624
[Bear] Come on.

00:00:26.585 --> 00:00:28.670
[Gordon Ramsay] [bleep] Come on.

00:00:28.754 --> 00:00:30.130
[Bear] Oh!

00:00:46.438 --> 00:00:47.481
[Gordon Ramsay] Right now,
I'm between

00:00:47.606 --> 00:00:49.232
mainland Florida and Cuba.

00:00:49.316 --> 00:00:51.735
And trust me, the waters
here are so shallow,

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:55.155
and they're filled
with coral reefs.

00:00:55.530 --> 00:00:57.616
Now, over the past
few centuries,

00:00:57.699 --> 00:00:59.868
they've claimed
over 1,000 boats.

00:00:59.951 --> 00:01:02.621
I just hope I don't
add to that list today.

00:01:02.954 --> 00:01:04.414
I'm in the Florida Keys,

00:01:04.456 --> 00:01:06.750
a series of 1,700
islands that extend over

00:01:06.792 --> 00:01:09.961
100 miles out into
the Gulf of Mexico.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.923
This area is so removed from
the mainland that locals have

00:01:12.964 --> 00:01:16.385
their own name for it,
the Conch Republic.

00:01:18.136 --> 00:01:20.389
I'm here to meet
Chef Paul Menta.

00:01:20.472 --> 00:01:22.974
Now, according to my GPS,

00:01:23.058 --> 00:01:25.602
he wanted to
meet me right here.

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:29.022
But honestly, it seems like
we're in the middle of nowhere.

00:01:29.147 --> 00:01:31.566
Where is this guy?

00:01:33.193 --> 00:01:35.654
Seriously?

00:01:35.737 --> 00:01:37.489
[bleep] no.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:42.327
That's not him.
No, surely not.

00:01:45.497 --> 00:01:48.834
[bleep]. What the?

00:01:57.676 --> 00:02:01.263
[bleep] hell.
You're crazy!

00:02:01.513 --> 00:02:03.890
Standing in the middle of
the Florida Keys and all of a

00:02:04.015 --> 00:02:05.851
sudden this bird flies over me.

00:02:05.976 --> 00:02:08.520
What in the heck is going on?

00:02:09.020 --> 00:02:11.148
This guy means business,
let me tell you.

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:13.608
He is not messing around.

00:02:18.447 --> 00:02:19.489
Trust me, he's the real deal.

00:02:19.656 --> 00:02:22.033
I mean, if he can show off
like that to meet me, that man,

00:02:22.159 --> 00:02:24.870
he's got some balls,
let me tell you.

00:02:32.544 --> 00:02:33.712
Paul!

00:02:33.879 --> 00:02:34.504
[Paul Menta] Hey, hey.

00:02:34.796 --> 00:02:36.548
[Gordon Ramsay] What was
that flying over me?

00:02:36.631 --> 00:02:37.883
Can I bring it in?

00:02:37.966 --> 00:02:40.594
[Paul Menta] Yeah, just
let it glide in, man.

00:02:40.844 --> 00:02:42.512
It's really shallow in here.

00:02:42.596 --> 00:02:45.849
[Gordon Ramsay] Man. Geez.
Good to see you, bud.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.184
[Paul Menta] Good to see you.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:49.853
-That was crazy.
-Yeah.

00:02:49.936 --> 00:02:53.482
[Gordon Ramsay] Paul Menta is a
true Keys culinary connoisseur.

00:02:55.066 --> 00:02:56.735
In his 30 years
living in the Keys,

00:02:56.818 --> 00:02:58.403
he has served as a chef
at several of the finest

00:02:58.487 --> 00:03:01.281
establishments in
the Conch Republic.

00:03:01.573 --> 00:03:03.825
Co-founded three local
eateries and opened up

00:03:03.909 --> 00:03:07.162
a sustainable fish market
and a rum distillery.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:09.581
The only thing Paul hasn't
done is learn how to execute

00:03:09.706 --> 00:03:11.917
the subtle arrival.

00:03:12.667 --> 00:03:13.710
What a place.

00:03:13.752 --> 00:03:14.544
[Paul Menta] Crazy, right?

00:03:14.753 --> 00:03:16.338
The tides are crazy
like the people here.

00:03:16.421 --> 00:03:17.881
[Gordon Ramsay] That bloody
jump was crazy.

00:03:17.923 --> 00:03:19.591
What the hell's going
on here with the barrels?

00:03:19.674 --> 00:03:21.092
[Paul Menta] Doing a
little bit of work, too.

00:03:21.176 --> 00:03:22.511
Salt curing some barrels.

00:03:22.594 --> 00:03:24.304
Bring them back to the
distillery later and

00:03:24.429 --> 00:03:25.764
fill them up with some rum.

00:03:25.889 --> 00:03:27.057
[Gordon Ramsay] You're
actually salting rum.

00:03:27.098 --> 00:03:29.309
[Paul Menta] Yeah. Think about
it like we do as a chef, right?

00:03:29.434 --> 00:03:30.101
[Gordon Ramsay] Sure.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.187
[Paul Menta] Put salt water
in here, let that cure,

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:33.688
bring out all that flavor.

00:03:33.772 --> 00:03:34.606
[Gordon Ramsay] I love that.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:36.024
[Paul Menta] We got to get
them up on the beach.

00:03:36.107 --> 00:03:36.733
We can roll these up.

00:03:36.942 --> 00:03:38.318
-Just roll them.
-Let's get, yeah.

00:03:38.443 --> 00:03:40.278
Let's get these
smaller ones up here.

00:03:40.362 --> 00:03:43.156
Once I got that brine in there,
I know the wood's all opened up.

00:03:43.281 --> 00:03:46.076
All that vanilla and all
those things are exposed

00:03:46.159 --> 00:03:47.410
inside the wood.

00:03:47.494 --> 00:03:48.370
And then we get the
high proof in there.

00:03:48.453 --> 00:03:49.621
[Gordon Ramsay] Wow.

00:03:49.704 --> 00:03:51.206
What a great technique,
